## Tests

All four are in `crates/tools/tests/acceptance.rs`.

- `statics_the_pure_crates_hold_only_the_statics_rule_4_allows` runs the real tree against `RULE_4_STATICS`. It passes only when exactly the four allowed statics are found, so it also proves the scan reaches them.
- `statics_the_scan_finds_each_interior_static` is a text scan. It flags `thread_local!` statics (brace and paren forms), `static mut`, an `AtomicU32`, an `[AtomicBool; 2]`, an `&[AtomicU8]` and `K: Cell`. It does not flag `OnceLock`, a `LazyLock` whose initializer calls `Cell::new`, `[GridCell; 2]`, `'static` lifetimes, `static_flags` or `Static::new`.
- `statics_the_scan_skips_test_items_and_keeps_the_lines` checks three things. A `#[cfg(test)]` `use` and a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` are skipped. `#[cfg(any(test, …))]` is not. Lines after the skipped items keep their numbers.
- `statics_the_check_refuses_an_unlisted_static_in_each_pure_crate` plants files under a scratch root for each of the five crates:
  - A `thread_local!`, an `AtomicU32` static and a `static mut` are reported.
  - A `OnceLock` static, a `thread_local!` inside `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`, one under `src/testkit/` and one in `walk_tests.rs` are not.
  - `static_failure` returns the rule 4 message.
